					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13893018#post-4834756</guid>
				<title>SCP-5217: </title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13893018/scp-5217#post-4834756</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Thu, 03 Dec 2020 01:26:26 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Suspicious Mr Guy</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>3481354</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Some of the dialogue is a <em>bit</em> off, specifically the way Wakefield writes/talks and not just in a &quot;he's supposed to be creepy and make you uncomfortable&quot; way, more of a general feeling of it being a bit too much. Aside from that however, I think this manages to keep its tone fairly well and gives a good cross-section of the foundation and its inner personnel processes, and was an enjoyable read with an interesting conclusion. Not a lot of SCPs can get me to google &quot;Scottish Drowning Horse&quot; +1</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
